# CVE-2026-47884 / CVE-2026-47890 — CRITICAL — org.springframework:spring-webmvc
# Both fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4.x requires Java 21).
# transaction-service targets Java 17; Boot 4.x migration tracked separately.
# Accepted risk: these CVEs require XsltView-based endpoints which transaction-service
# does not expose.
# TODO: remove once transaction-service migrates to Java 21 + Spring Boot 4.x.
CVE-2026-47884
CVE-2026-47890

# CVE-2026-106449 / CVE-2026-59949 / CVE-2026-106450 / CVE-2026-106452 / CVE-2026-106453
# HIGH/MEDIUM — org.lz4:lz4-java 1.10.1 (transitive via kafka-clients in transaction-service)
# Trivy reports these as fixed in 1.11.x, but 1.11.x exists only in the at.yawk.lz4 fork;
# the canonical org.lz4:lz4-java in Maven Central is at 1.10.1 with no stable upgrade path.
# GitHub Code Scanning re-rates all five as LOW or MEDIUM.
# Accepted risk: lz4 is a codec used for Kafka message compression, not exposed externally.
# TODO: remove once kafka-clients ships with an updated lz4-java or org.lz4 releases 1.11.x.
CVE-2026-106449
CVE-2026-59949
CVE-2026-106450
CVE-2026-106452
CVE-2026-106453

# CVE-2026-106451 — HIGH — at.yawk.lz4:lz4-java (transitive via kafka-clients)
# Trivy sometimes matches the at.yawk.lz4 fork groupId separately. Same acceptance rationale.
CVE-2026-106451

# CVE-2026-54704 — MEDIUM — opentelemetry-javaagent (JDBC logging clear-text credentials)
# Fix is only available in 2.28.0-alpha (pre-release); no stable release yet.
# Mitigated: JDBC auto-instrumentation debug logging is disabled in production
# (JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS only activates the agent when explicitly set; debug logging off by default).
# TODO: remove once OTel Java instrumentation 2.28.0 stable is released.
CVE-2026-54704
